[
  {
    "name": "azul_widgets_touch_tabs_pictures_on_a_phone_at_its_own_size",
    "description": "The pictures of the tab strip on a phone, at the window's own size (no resize, no rotation: the phone is the window): the Pixel 8 preset (the strip in the status bar's band around the camera), a far pill selected (the row scrolls to put it whole in a lane), the end of the row, dark, flora, the phone it really runs on ('This phone': its own cutout, nothing simulated), a ribbon in the band, light and dark, and the page with no phone. Taken in this order: 1 Pixel 8 light flat, 2 Design selected, 3 Account selected, 4 dark, 5 flora light, 6 flora dark, 7 this phone, 8 ribbon in the band, 9 ribbon dark. A phone is turned by hand (or by the QA script) for the landscape pictures; the host scenario has them on a resized window.",
